romanized_response:
HTTP status code 429 Too Many Requests ante server lo edo oka rakamaina rate limit undani, mee request aa limit ni exceed chesindani artham. Idi kinda reasons lo edaina valla kavachu:

1. Ee request chese code ni chinna time period lo chala sarlu run chesaru, danivalla rate limit exceed ayindi.

2. Website ki spam laga anipinche requests ni 429 status code tho reject chestundi. Dini artham user agent common browser kakapovachu; idi konni websites use chese simple check. Dinni rectify cheyadaniki, GET request ki "User-Agent" header ni ila add cheyachu:

```
const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1', 
     { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'browser.version' }  }
);
```

Gamaninchandi, meeru `"browser.version"` ni actual browser user agent string tho replace cheyali. Ee code ye application lo run avutundo dani batti, idi user agent spoofing ga consider cheyabadachu; idi konni countries leda organizations laws prakaram (leda aa code access cheyadaniki try chestunna website terms of service prakaram) restricted ayi undachu.

3. Website inkoka reason valla requests ni rate limit chestundi. Request proxy dwara velladam valla idi kavachu; ala ayithe aa proxy ni use chese vere users chala ekkuva requests chesi undachu, ayina idi unlikely.

4. Website denial of service attack lo undadam valla anni requests ni reject chestundi. Idi unlikely, endukante alanti attack lo server typical behavior traffic ni non-existent server ki route cheyadam leda poorthiga deny cheyadam, valid response em ivvakapovadam. Ayithe website HTTP status code tho respond chesina kuda, server overload ayinappudu iche server error 503 Service Unavailable ayye chance ekkuva.

response_en:
Yes, certainly! The issue you're encountering is because the string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", and "buzz" are temporary values, and you are trying to return a reference to them, which is not allowed because they will be dropped at the end of the scope, and the returned reference would be dangling.

You can fix this error by returning &'static str instead of &str. &'static str refers to string literals, which have a 'static lifetime, meaning they last for the duration of the program. Here's an updated version of your code:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note that the last arm returns a &'static str that is created from a String using the Box::leak function, which takes ownership of a Box<T> and returns a pointer to its contents, effectively leaking it. This is safe because the returned pointer will last for the duration of the program, but it should be used with care as it will not be cleaned up automatically.

romanized_response:
Avunu, tappakunda! Meeru face chestunna issue enti ante, "fizzbuzz", "fizz", mariyu "buzz" ane string literals temporary values, mariyu meeru vatiki reference return cheyyadaniki try chestunnaru. Adi allowed kaadu, endukante avi scope end lo drop avutayi, appudu return chesina reference dangling avutundi.

Ee error ni fix cheyyadaniki &str badulu &'static str return cheyyachu. &'static str ante string literals ni refer chestundi; vatiki 'static lifetime untundi, ante program duration mottam avi untayi. Mee code yokka updated version ikkada undi:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Last arm oka &'static str return chestundani gamaninchandi. Adi Box::leak function use chesi String nunchi create chestaru. Ee function Box<T> ownership teesukoni, dani contents ki pointer return chestundi, effectively danini leak chestundi. Idi safe, endukante returned pointer program duration mottam untundi, kani jagrattaga use cheyyali, endukante idi automatic ga clean up avvadu.

response_en:
Merge sort is a divide and conquer algorithm that works by recursively splitting the input array in half until the arrays are split into single elements. Then, the sorted arrays are merged back together in sorted order.

The key benefits of merge sort over a simpler algorithm like bubble sort are:

1. It is a stable sort that does not change the relative order of elements with equal keys.
2. It has an efficiency of O(n log n) time complexity, making it a relatively efficient algorithm even for large input sizes. Bubble sort, on the other hand, has a quadratic time complexity of O(n^2), making it very inefficient for larger inputs.
3. It is a generic algorithm that can sort any type of data for which a comparison function exists.

Here is a Rust implementation example:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
    if vec.len() < 2 {
        return;
    }

    let mid = vec.len() / 2;
    let (left, right) = vec.split_at_mut(mid);

    merge_sort(left);
    merge_sort(right);

    merge(left, right, vec);
}

fn merge(left: &mut [i32], right: &mut [i32], vec: &mut [i32]) {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = 0;
    let mut k = 0;

    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] < right[j] {
            vec[k] = left[i];
            i += 1;
        } else {
            vec[k] = right[j];
            j += 1;
        }
        k += 1;
    }

    while i < left.len() {
        vec[k] = left[i];
        i += 1;
        k += 1;
    }

    while j < right.len() {
        vec[k] = right[j];
        j += 1;
        k += 1;
    }
}
```

romanized_response:
Merge sort anedi divide and conquer algorithm. Idi input array ni recursively sagam sagam ga split chesthu, arrays single elements ga split ayye varaku pani chestundi. Tarvata, sorted arrays ni sorted order lo malli merge chestundi.

Bubble sort laanti simpler algorithm tho compare cheste merge sort yokka key benefits ive:

1. Idi stable sort, ante equal keys unna elements relative order ni marchadu.
2. Daani efficiency O(n log n) time complexity, kabatti large input sizes ki kuda idi relatively efficient algorithm. Maro vaipu, bubble sort ki O(n^2) ane quadratic time complexity untundi, kabatti larger inputs ki adi chala inefficient.
3. Idi generic algorithm, comparison function unna e type data aina sort cheyyagaladu.

Ikkada oka Rust implementation example undi:
```rust
